WEBVTT

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.760
Hold your breath for a while.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.530
It's an awful smell.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.140
Where did Soun disappear to?

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.900
I wonder if the banquet's started already.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:47.890
Where will the banquet be held?

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.030
In Jyurojin's train.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:03.220
"Nasebanaru" to hito wa yuuga

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:03.220
People say, "Where there's 
a will, there's a way"

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.780
Narugamama naseba ii

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:06.780
But things can just be how they'll be

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.250
Nagareru kawa ukabu kobune

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.250
A small boat floats along the river

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:23.180
Doko ni yukuno darouka

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:23.180
I wonder where it's going

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:28.370
Ikisaki nado yosou dekinu

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:28.370
I can't even guess its destination

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:32.650
Sorega omoshiroki koto

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:32.650
But that's why it's so fun

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:41.780
Kokorozashi wa takaku mokuhyou wa hikuku

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:41.780
My intentions are high, but my goals are low

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:46.790
Aho wo mazerya kekka

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:46.790
When foolishness gets mixed in

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:54.460
Yukai ni nareru

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:54.470
Everything will be merry

00:01:55.930 --> 00:02:00.610
Narugamama ni sawagu mama ni

00:01:55.930 --> 00:02:00.610
As things will be, as chaotic as they will be

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:05.310
Toraburu suramo nenryou sa

00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:05.310
Even troubles become fuel

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:09.780
Namikaze tatanai jinsei wa

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:09.780
A life lived without any strife

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.280
Chotto bakkari tsumaranai

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:14.280
Can be a bit boring

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.010
Okiraku ni gokuraku ni

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:19.010
Carefree and blissfully

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:23.560
Kaze ni makasete ikou

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:23.560
Let's let the wind lead us

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:28.000
Kyou mo bakashite ikou

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:28.000
Let's go trick everyone again today

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.000
<b>Episode Seven
The Friday Club Once More</b>

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.630
Ow...

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.070
I've returned.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.060
Well, well...

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.820
Who might this be?

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:04.060
My name is Shimogamo Yasaburo.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.680
Do you remember him?

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.000
From the end of last year
at Chitoseya in Ponto-cho.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.620
He's a very amusing boy.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Being amusing is a good thing.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:19.090
I just happened to run into him in Hell.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:21.700
Apparently, Ebisugawa kicked him down there.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:26.010
Oh, my. Now that's
quite a devilish thing to do.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.920
It must've been fate that
I ran into him down there.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:32.650
Would you allow him to participate
in the banquet, as well?

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:37.110
I'm sure no one would decline
a request from you, Benten-san.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:44.320
I'm sure it must have
been rather frightful.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:51.960
It's not as though I leave
the painting of Hell openly accessible.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.980
There aren't many that come back
after entering this painting.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:00.530
The only one who goes back and forth
effortlessly is Benten-san.

00:04:00.530 --> 00:04:04.180
The only thing more fearsome
than the painting of Hell is Benten-san.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.180
I heard that.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:15.740
This painting is so frightful
that I asked a certain artist to change it.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:20.900
Now, because of his Buddha,
I can admire the painting without worry.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.110
Does Hell scare even someone like yourself?

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.230
Of course.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:29.430
It feels as though I'm looking
at my own insides.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.710
Why don't you two make use
of the outdoor baths before the banquet?

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:40.080
The smell of Hell will get in the way
of the taste of alcohol.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.890
<b>Women</b>

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.890
<b>Men</b>

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.230
My name is Yasaburo. Pardon me.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:06.920
Well, hello, Yasaburo-kun
of the Thursday Club.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.660
Hey, Yodogawa-san, your friend has arrived.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:15.830
Now the Thursday Club
and the Friday Club finally meet.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:19.640
Did they manage to coerce you
with the outdoor bath and coffee milk?

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.370
You're strongly mistaken

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:25.050
if you think that they can buy me off
with a Sunshine Policy like this.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:28.870
But outdoor baths are such a wonderful thing.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:32.550
They bring out the true worth
of coffee milk this much.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.590
What do you plan to do next?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.680
I'm planning a huge speech at the banquet.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:41.650
I'm going all in.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.990
Could you not do your scheming
while we're here?

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:49.120
Please don't forget that tonight's banquet
will be one of reconciliation.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:52.150
I never said I'd be willing to reconcile.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:55.000
Just how stubborn are you?

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.600
Let's just enjoy ourselves, Yodogawa-san.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:01.880
Yes, especially since we're welcoming 
our new Hotei-san tonight.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:06.140
This is such a lovely bath.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.720
Well, hello. Nice to meet you.

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:18.290
How's the water, everyone?

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:27.060
Nothing is better than the hot springs
with a beautiful woman.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.950
I have discovered that Heaven
is truly in the hot springs.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.940
Such a lovely bath.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:37.920
Hey, now. Goodness, your desires
are written all over your face.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:42.330
I understand how you feel,
but you need to hold back.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.100
Pardon me.

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:01.520
Hey, Yasaburo-kun. We meet again.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:05.020
Tenmaya-san...
I'm surprised you're still alive.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.850
The day I die is the day this world ends.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.490
Are you working for Jyurojin again?

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:17.620
<b>Trick Denki Bran</b>

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.970
I'm back to being a dog on a leash.

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:17.010
Either I'm very capable,

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:19.830
or my boss is feeling whimsical.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:28.530
Tonight, we welcome a new Hotei
and meet face to face with the Thursday Club.

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:32.470
Let us hope it will be a pleasant evening.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.830
So then, cheers.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.470
Cheers.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.340
Let me pour you a drink.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.980
Why, thank you.

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.730
You seem rather pleased, Ebisugawa-san.

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:53.360
Well, I am being invited
to join the Friday Club.

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:57.560
It's such an honor that
there's no way I wouldn't be happy.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:07:59.920
You'll be able to eat
all the tanuki you want.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.710
So much, you might end up growing a tail.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.210
Allow me to entertain you tonight.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:12.720
Here we go.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:17.340
Gentlemen, please observe this rock.

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:23.190
Oh, that's a cute little rock.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.700
Water.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.620
Water's coming out from that pebble.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:36.690
I found these dragon stones
at the head of the Kamo River,

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:41.060
and, miraculously,
water always flows from them.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:46.920
I've heard that there are
tiny dragons living within the stones.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:51.220
I present this to you tonight, Jyurojin-sama.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.590
Well, that's rather kind of you.

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:58.550
Oh, this is but a token of my gratitude.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:01.560
Please, take it.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:11.150
I shall present this to Benten-san.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.170
Oh, are you sure?

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:16.490
Well, it was given to me.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.160
Er, uh...

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:25.800
Gentlemen, let us toast in welcoming

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:29.440
Ebisugawa-san into the Friday Club.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:31.000
Yes, let's!

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.100
Objection!

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.260
Huh?

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.980
Ebisugawa-san, it's not too late.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:39.720
You shouldn't join the Friday Club.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:43.060
Eating tanuki hot pot is
truly a savage thing to do.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.280
But, Yodogawa-sensei,

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:49.650
you ate quite a few of them yourself.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:54.060
That's right, Yodogawa-san.
In fact, you've eaten more than I have.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:59.000
You've been cast out of the club.
Do you even have the right to object?

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:04.120
You sophists have such a terrible habit
of objecting to every little thing.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:08.200
After enjoying the hot springs
in Arima, coffee milk,

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.430
and partaking in this feast,

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:14.130
having the audacity to call us savages

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:15.630
is rather annoying.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:19.190
Those are two separate matters.

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:21.770
That's because hot springs, coffee milk,

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:24.540
and this feast are all a matter of desire,

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.540
while tanuki hot pots are a matter of love!

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:31.580
Oh, here we go again, Professor Sophistry.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:34.380
We've had enough of your arguments.

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:38.220
Also, could you stop throwing around
that defamatory material? It's embarrassing.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:41.520
It's your choice not to eat
tanuki hot pot, Yodogawa-san.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:44.910
But it's also our choice
to eat tanuki hot pot.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.410
Why do you try to force your love upon us?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.730
That's because love is something
that you force upon others.

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.170
It's true that I've eaten tanuki.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.090
That's because that's
how I expressed my love back then.

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:00.520
But I was wrong, so I apologize.

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:04.810
All I can do now is act
as a preacher of tanuki love

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:07.060
and protest the
Friday Club's evil traditions.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:11.090
Are you saying that I don't have
the right to try to persuade you all

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:12.910
because I've eaten tanuki hot pots myself?

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:14.900
Then let me just say this...

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:18.110
I don't plan on persuading any of you.

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:21.860
I'm just going to influence you.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.800
That's a rather dangerous idea.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:24.990
I can't keep up with you.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:30.290
Calm down, now. Yodogawa-san,
you're really on edge right now.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:32.120
Love is illogical.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.540
Is that what you're trying to say, Sensei?

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:38.150
That's exactly right, Benten-san!

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:40.760
Perhaps you can understand
what I'm trying to say?

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:44.430
Are you saying that you have
no intentions of backing down?

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.210
I will not!

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:53.300
Three generations of the Yodogawa family

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:55.890
has enjoyed tanuki hot pots with us,

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:57.640
so this is truly unfortunate.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:11:59.190
Tenmaya.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.010
<b>Hell Sumo Hall</b>

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.010
<b>Tenmaya Ramen Shop</b>

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:22.010
<b>Inogashira Hell Station</b>

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:36.310
Is there a tanuki more important
than your life?

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:38.500
Wait, Jyurojin! Hold on a second!

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.560
Guns are a bad idea!

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:42.190
Blood! There will be blood!

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:44.400
I have plenty of bullets.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:45.450
I can shoot as much as I please.

00:12:46.610 --> 00:12:47.660
Please wait!

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.960
Did you need something, Yasaburo-kun?

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:54.650
There's something I'd like
to say to Professor Yodogawa.

00:12:58.640 --> 00:13:01.430
It's true that I became
close to you as a member

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.710
of the Thursday Club.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:06.760
But to tell you the truth,

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:10.720
I've become sick of your tanuki love.

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:16.100
The only reason I decided to hang around
was so you would keep feeding me.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:20.530
But despite the delicious food you've fed me,

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:23.730
I can't keep up with your
warped sense of love.

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.950
I've finally realized today
that I've reached my limit.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:29.590
But...

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:32.950
Please don't say such harsh things.

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:37.870
I am declaring my withdrawal from
the Thursday Club right here, right now.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:42.960
If your delusional tanuki love
is going to keep causing everyone trouble,

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:44.880
then I will stop you myself.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:49.950
That will be my atonement
to everyone in the Friday Club

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:52.430
for all the trouble you've caused them.

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:57.430
Ah, I've had enough of your forcing
your nonsensical sophistic love on others.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:00.560
I have my own vision of love.

00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:04.950
Wh-What a very logical young man.

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:07.820
Well said, 21st-century boy!

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.230
Hear! Hear!

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:15.750
Well said! Let us have a toast
to this boy's resolve.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:18.430
But we were comrades.

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:22.180
We spoke so much about our mutual love
for how cute tanuki were.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:26.440
To be honest, I'm extremely interested
in tanuki hot pots.

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.340
Wh-What?!

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:32.530
You're the one who pressed the idea
that to eat is to love.

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.370
Come to think of it,

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:38.920
ever since I was invited
to the Friday Club's banquet last fall,

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:43.590
there hasn't been a moment
when I wasn't thinking about tanuki hot pots.

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:46.390
I haven't been able
to hold back my fascination

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:48.360
with the Friday Club's mystical tradition

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:53.400
in which they eat such a brutish
and bizarre dish without a care

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:55.010
about how it looks to the public.

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:58.370
Then why don't you just join the Friday Club?

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:06.800
W-Wait—

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:08.180
Tenmaya!

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:11.760
Yes, ma'am, you got it.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.230
Benten-sama, that's—

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:20.540
Hush, boy.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:44.500
Hey, we're flying.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.740
This is...

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:47.800
Well...

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:49.760
Well, I'll be.

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:54.220
Oho...

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:59.820
This is a gift for Jyurojin
from Yasaburo and myself.

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:09.230
This is a present worthy
of my 120th birthday.

00:16:12.270 --> 00:16:14.960
I shall welcome you into the seat of Hotei.

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:17.290
Welcome to the Friday Club.

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:32.510
What kind of farce is this?

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:34.840
What's the matter, Ebisugawa?

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.680
Do you have a problem with this?

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:40.790
This is far too cruel!

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:44.970
We were supposed to be welcoming me
into the Friday Club tonight!

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:47.900
Well, plans do change, at times.

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:52.510
But... But... Why does it have to be him?!

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:54.080
You are being fooled.

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:55.430
You're all being fooled!

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:58.160
He is a terrible villain!

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.230
And that's perfectly fine.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:03.500
I happen to enjoy the company of villains.

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:07.170
Let's just say that
it wasn't meant to be this time.

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:09.840
Cheer up.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.480
I'll hear you out if you need an ear.

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:17.510
Then I would like for you
to return the dragon stone.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:20.010
But I've given that to Benten-san.

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.970
What's mine is mine.

00:17:22.970 --> 00:17:25.480
Well, there you have it, Ebisugawa.

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.730
You monsters...

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.670
I've listened to countless demands from you.

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:36.200
Do you know how much anguish
you've caused me?

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:41.990
I've worked thousands of times harder
than that slacker Yasaburo!

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:46.210
Why do you want to join
the Friday Club so much?

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.600
I just...

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:53.670
I just wanted to strike down
those filthy tanuki.

00:17:53.980 --> 00:17:57.380
Are you saying that you want
to become an oni yourself?

00:17:57.810 --> 00:18:01.140
Strike down... Strike down...

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:08.930
W-Wait! Wait!

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:14.070
Yasaburo, how much more
do you plan to get in my way?!

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:17.070
Don't transform!

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:23.740
M-Monster, begone! Monster, begone!

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.080
Tenmaya!

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:30.560
D-Don't shoot...

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.540
Don't shoot!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:46.580
To think that he was actually a monster...

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:49.520
It's not surprising for an oni to appear.

00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:53.640
After all, Hell lies
right under these hot springs.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:55.640
Ow...

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.210
Soun...

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:18.420
Soun, where are you?

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:25.930
Then I'll do what I must
to survive in this foreign land.

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:42.240
Behold my end.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:48.580
Apparently, I didn't even have
what it took to be an oni.

00:19:54.150 --> 00:19:59.090
In the end, both heroes and villains
are naught but furballs.

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:01.070
Don't die in a place like this.

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:03.090
I'm going to take you home with me.

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:07.620
You've avenged your father.

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:09.970
You should be happier than this.

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:12.500
What are you doing, Uncle?

00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:14.650
This is far too pitiful.

00:20:15.570 --> 00:20:18.320
Ebisugawa Soun...

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:22.700
embarks now for the realm of the dead.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:31.940
Uncle...

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:36.140
I didn't want things to end like this...

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:43.630
But at the same time,
I can't tell you exactly what I wanted.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:45.010
But...

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:50.640
Is that my father?

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:55.090
Is that you, Kaisei?

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:59.700
Yasaburo, why are you crying?

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:03.490
That's my father there, right?

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:07.390
He was shot by Tenmaya.

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:10.550
Is it bad?

00:21:12.210 --> 00:21:15.290
He's not suffering anymore.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:24.650
Would you leave me alone
with my father for a bit?

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:31.760
Thanks, Yasaburo...

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:40.000
<i>Only a gaunt, poor-looking tanuki lay there.</i>

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:45.860
<i>My rage that was once so strong
that I thought I could hold it in my hands</i>

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:48.550
<i>was now slipping away into nothingness.</i>

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:53.420
<i>In the end, both heroes and villains
are naught but furballs,</i>

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:58.020
<i>and all furballs go to Heaven.</i>

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:09.310
Tsuki wo medetewa toki ni wa nusunde

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:09.310
While gazing lovingly at the 
moon, at times, she steals it

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:14.140
Whimsical as she may be, ah

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:14.140
Kimagure na kanojo wa ah

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:18.610
Kawabe de hitori hoho ni namida

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:18.610
As she stands by the riverside 
alone, secretly her tears

00:22:18.610 --> 00:22:22.960
Utsukushiku tayutau

00:22:18.610 --> 00:22:22.960
Quiver beautifully upon her cheeks

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:34.750
Boku no te tori nagara 
kokoro wa dokoka ni ukabu

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:34.750
She takes my hand, as her 
heart floats away somewhere

00:22:34.750 --> 00:22:39.250
Kasaneta te ni wa mada nukumori

00:22:34.750 --> 00:22:39.250
I still feel that warmth from her held hand

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:43.630
Setsunai yume no sono ato saki

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:43.630
Somewhere beyond this sentimental dream

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:53.250
Demo kimi no me wa harukana 
mirai wo miteitane

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:53.250
But you were already looking 
far into the future

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:57.920
Zutto zutto oikaketayo

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:57.920
I always chased after you

00:22:57.920 --> 00:23:02.270
Kimi ga kizutsuku toki mo

00:22:57.920 --> 00:23:02.270
Even when you were hurt

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:11.640
Sotto mabuta ni yakitsuita kimi no sugata ni

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:11.640
The vision of you that's 
softly imprinted on my eyes

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:16.560
Ima mata tooku e to ah

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:16.560
Once again, you fly far away, ah

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:29.000
Tondeiku kimi wa hora Kanata no hito

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:29.000
You are a person far beyond

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.340
This is so annoying.

00:23:33.340 --> 00:23:35.830
Seriously, just give me a break.

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:40.290
I already have enough trouble
dealing with my idiot brothers.

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Episode Eight
Ebisugawa Kaisei's Secret</b>
